@c ====================================================================
@node Needs
@chapter Needs

@cindex needs
@emph{Players and preservationists} want to play the classic id Tech 1
games on current Linux systems with vanilla behaviour: the same
physics, the same monster behaviour, the same random sequence, so that
historic demos play back and speedrun records stay checkable.  They
supply their own IWADs and expect the engine to find them, play every
map, and never crash on a malformed PWAD.

@emph{The maintainer} wants a complete id Tech 1 port in safe Rust, as
a showcase.  The simulation shall have no @code{unsafe}, and every
claim of fidelity shall be backed by a test anyone can rerun.  No
existing Rust effort has shipped all of @cite{Doom} through
@cite{Final Doom}.  room4doom comes closest and still lacks the cast
call and the automap.

