@c ====================================================================
@node Principles
@chapter Principles

@cindex principles
@cindex determinism
@enumerate
@item
@strong{Correctness before cleverness.}  Where gameplay depends on a
behaviour, vanilla behaviour wins, including documented bugs.
@item
@strong{Determinism is the contract.}  The simulation has a fixed 35 Hz
tic, 16.16 fixed-point maths with explicit wrapping, the original
random tables, a stable iteration order, and no wall-clock time,
floating point, or renderer state.
@item
@strong{Presentation never feeds back.}  Renderers, audio, and UI read
a snapshot of the simulation and never change it.
@item
@strong{Evidence over assertion.}  Each fidelity claim names the test
that proves it.
@item
@strong{Untrusted by default.}  Every byte of a WAD, demo, or save is
parsed with checked bounds into typed errors.
@end enumerate

