@node Risks
@chapter Risks

@cindex risks
@multitable @columnfractions .3 .1 .12 .48
@headitem Risk @tab Impact @tab Likelihood @tab Mitigation
@item Demo desync from subtle order or overflow differences
@tab High @tab High
@tab Per-tic checksums, Chocolate Doom oracle, @code{demo diff}
first-divergence tool, transliteration that keeps call order.
@item Thinker or link order lost when pointers become handles
@tab High @tab Medium
@tab Index-linked lists in the arena; golden traces on monster-heavy
maps.
@item Vanilla undefined behaviour (freed @code{target}, overflows) is
relied on by demos
@tab Medium @tab Medium
@tab Emulate the observable result explicitly; R-040 optional overflow
emulation.
@item Commercial IWADs absent from CI
@tab Medium @tab Certain
@tab Freedoom and shareware in CI; a scripted local acceptance run
before each release.
@item Young OPL crate
@tab Medium @tab Medium
@tab §24 audit; fallback is porting Nuked OPL3 in tree, keeping its
LGPL-2.1-or-later notice (§4.2).
@item wgpu API churn
@tab Low @tab High
@tab Presenter stays thin; @code{softbuffer} fallback; versions pinned.
@item Scope creep toward Boom or ZDoom
@tab High @tab High
@tab NG-1; DeHackEd is the only extension format.
@item Trademark complaint
@tab Medium @tab Low
@tab Codename, no assets, no logos, disclaimer.
@end multitable

